{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SuYtNaPmTCTEiiAL12pRWu","type":"tool_result","content":"282:[Omitted long matching line]\n365:That one fact is the premise of Chapter 9. When you get to Services, the entire argument for why they must exist rests on the Pod having an IP that changes when the Pod is replaced *[cross-bearing: see Ch 9 — why a Service is necessary]*.\n476:- **\"They reach each other through a Service\"** describes how containers in *different* Pods communicate. Containers in the same Pod need no such thing; a Service in front of your own sidecar is a network hop that buys nothing.\n827:             │ running?                │ container → restart  │ Service endpoints\n858:[Omitted long matching line]\n1093:Now go back to where you started this chapter. If \"Pod is Kubernetes' word for container\" had been true, **every single one of those seven statements would be wrong.** Not subtly wrong. Wrong in ways that produce confidently incorrect answers about IP addressing, about restart behavior, about what a status field is describing, and about what a Service is pointed at.\n1150:A) A Service and a ConfigMap\n1249:D) Both: the container is killed and the Pod is removed from Service endpoints\n1253:A) The Pod's IP is removed from Service endpoints; the container keeps running\n1344:[Omitted long matching line]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"452dc64f-97ea-42e9-8053-7210317581e0","uuid":"1a866859-df03-447e-bbf7-6f9a4bbe3463","timestamp":"2026-08-24T12:58:34.602Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"282:[Omitted long matching line]\n365:That one fact is the premise of Chapter 9. When you get to Services, the entire argument for why they must exist rests on the Pod having an IP that changes when the Pod is replaced *[cross-bearing: see Ch 9 — why a Service is necessary]*.\n476:- **\"They reach each other through a Service\"** describes how containers in *different* Pods communicate. Containers in the same Pod need no such thing; a Service in front of your own sidecar is a network hop that buys nothing.\n827:             │ running?                │ container → restart  │ Service endpoints\n858:[Omitted long matching line]\n1093:Now go back to where you started this chapter. If \"Pod is Kubernetes' word for container\" had been true, **every single one of those seven statements would be wrong.** Not subtly wrong. Wrong in ways that produce confidently incorrect answers about IP addressing, about restart behavior, about what a status field is describing, and about what a Service is pointed at.\n1150:A) A Service and a ConfigMap\n1249:D) Both: the container is killed and the Pod is removed from Service endpoints\n1253:A) The Pod's IP is removed from Service endpoints; the container keeps running\n1344:[Omitted long matching line]","numLines":10,"totalLines":10}}
