s what it will accept. You've already met the mechanism in disguise: the DaemonSet's tolerations in §7 were a node saying \"not for general traffic\" and a controller saying \"this one's an exception.\"\n1211:Chapter 6 complete. You came in able to read a Pod and left able to author a fleet — six workload resources, one control loop, and the beginning of the recognition that the loop is the whole system rather than a feature of it.\n1214:*Part II, Chapter 6 of 18. The trunk of the book is behind you.*","numLines":54,"totalLines":54}}
